{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe Gerrit Verified gate executes workflow files from TRUSTED MAIN, not the patchset (proven\non change 2115 PS1: its own run 32587991195 still executed main's stale `--timeout=20`,\nheadSha 6a5c88027c5). pytest-timeout precedence is marker > CLI > `PYTEST_TIMEOUT` env > ini\n(`get_env_settings` / `_get_item_settings` in `pytest_timeout.py`), so the\n`--timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread` CLI flags on `_build-and-test.yml`'s two shared-tier\nlanes (the default-suite and integration `run:` commands) permanently shadow any future\nper-test-budget change carried in `pyproject.toml`: a budget fix can never be exercised by its\nown Verified run — the class of failure that made 2115 PS1 fail its own gate. Bug\n`3fa7-94ba-42aa-4623` was ultimately landed by an operator-cast Verified+1, which is not a\nrepeatable path.\n\n## Approach\n\nSingle-source the shared-tier budget: REMOVE the `--timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread` CLI\nflags from both `_build-and-test.yml` lanes and let `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` (`timeout =\n300`, `timeout_method = \"thread\"`, at `pyproject.toml:662-663`) govern. This is the\necosystem-standard shape — scikit-learn, pandas and numpy pass no `--timeout` on their CI\npytest command lines; the budget lives in config. With the flags gone, a patchset that changes\nthe ini budget IS exercised by its own Verified run, because the ini travels with the patchset\nwhile workflow files come from trusted main.\n\nEffective budgets do not change: the lanes ran at CLI `--timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread`\nand the ini already carries the identical values, so removal only moves authority (the\nbefore/after is documented in the commit message). The eleven other `--timeout=` lanes\n(external-integration, optionality, eval-discipline, test.yml, structured-output-baseline)\nkeep their own larger calibrated CLI budgets — they drive live services, clean-venv installs\nand eval sweeps, and several run outside this repo's rootdir where the ini is not in play.\n\nThe previously drafted conftest-floor mechanism (branch `preserve/timeout-floor-hardening`,\ncommit `b38bf9a4748`) is rejected and does not land: pytest-timeout resolves\n`config._env_timeout` at session start read-only, so a conftest floor has no supported hook\npoint and no OSS precedent. That branch is mined for its reusable test assets only (the\nparity-contract rewrites and the lane-flag removals); its `tests/_timeout_floor.py`, conftest\nhook, and docs floor section are discarded, and the branch (local-only; it has no `origin`\nref) is deleted after mining.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` — remove `--timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread`\n  from the default-suite and integration `run:` commands; rewrite the adjacent hang-guard\n  comments to say the budget lives in the ini and these lanes are deliberately flag-free.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` — rewrite\n  `test_the_shared_tier_lanes_carry_the_ini_timeout_budget` to assert the two shared-tier\n  lanes carry NO `--timeout`/`--timeout-method` flags (and that the ini budget is present and\n  positive, since it becomes their only guard); update\n  `test_every_ci_pytest_lane_has_a_per_test_hang_guard` so a lane may satisfy the guard by\n  inheriting the asserted-real ini keys (budget positive, `thread` method) instead of an\n  explicit flag, while a lane that DOES set a flag must still use the `thread` method.\n- `docs/local-dev-env.md` — update the sentence stating the two lanes are \"held equal to the\n  ini value\" to say they are held flag-free (single-sourced from the ini).\n\n## Testing\n\nRED-first: the rewritten parity contract asserting no `--timeout`/`--timeout-method` on the\nshared-tier lanes is the oracle — it fails against the current workflow (flags present) and\npasses after the removal. The hang-guard sweep keeps its negative power: it still requires\nevery other pytest lane to carry an explicit budget flag with the `thread` method, and the ini\nfallback it now accepts for flag-free lanes is asserted real (`timeout` positive,\n`timeout_method = \"thread\"`) rather than assumed. An unmarked hung test remains bounded: the\nout-of-process negative arms in `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py` prove the ini keys alone\nexpire a hung body, setup, and teardown. `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the targeted\nsuites (`pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py`) run\ngreen before push.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Neither `_build-and-test.yml` shared-tier lane passes `--timeout` or `--timeout-method`\n      on its pytest command line; checked by the rewritten parity contract failing if a flag\n      reappears.\n- [ ] The ini remains the lanes' real guard: the parity contracts assert\n      `[tool.pytest.ini_options].timeout` is present and positive and `timeout_method` is\n      `thread`, and the existing out-of-process negative arms in `test_timeout_budget.py`\n      prove those keys alone expire a hung test (no weakening of the hang guard).\n- [ ] The hang-guard sweep still requires an explicit `--timeout` flag (with\n      `--timeout-method=thread`) on every pytest lane outside `_build-and-test.yml`; checked\n      by `test_every_ci_pytest_lane_has_a_per_test_hang_guard` passing over the unchanged\n      eleven calibrated lanes.\n- [ ] The effective shared-tier budget is unchanged (300 s, thread method, before and after);\n      documented in the commit message and checked by the ini config arm in\n      `test_timeout_budget.py` still pinning `timeout = 300`.\n- [ ] Branch `preserve/timeout-floor-hardening` is deleted after mining (local `git branch -D`;\n      it has no `origin` ref, verified via `git ls-remote origin 'refs/heads/preserve/*'`);\n      recorded in this ticket's close evidence.","title":"Single-source the shared-tier hang budget in the ini; remove the CI CLI --timeout flags"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787449660263140001,"uuid":"b3f636af-7184-4ae9-b77c-d389f830b8b3"}